{
  "moduleId": "nec-projectors",
  "name": "NEC Projectors",
  "repo": "bitfocus/companion-module-nec-projectors",
  "version": "1.1.0",
  "baseVersion": "2.0.4",
  "lastCommit": "2026-10-07",
  "lastCommitSha": "6cee647",
  "status": "verified-sample",
  "coverage": "complete",
  "notes": [
    "Complete list: 22 actions (src/actions.ts, one setActionDefinitions call) and 12 boolean feedbacks (src/feedbacks.ts, one setFeedbackDefinitions call). Choice lists come from src/nec/constants.ts; nothing is generated per model at runtime.",
    "Transport: HTTP to the projector's IsapiExtPj.dll control CGI (default port 80, optional password logon with cookie and md5 nonce handshake; src/nec/client.ts, src/config.ts). Binary command bytes are sent through that HTTP interface (src/nec/protocol.ts).",
    "Built on @companion-module/base 2.0.4, so option values may be expressions, except in fields marked disableAutoExpression (the input, aspect, eco and audio source dropdowns, which also offer the sentinel id 'custom').",
    "Dropdown ids keep the source type: most lists use numeric ids (hex literals in the source, recorded as decimal numbers, for example 0x7f = 127, 0xff = 255); the input, aspect, eco and audio-source lists mix numbers with the string id 'custom'. Choosing 'custom' enables a hex text field (custom, inputCustom, sourceCustom) that parseHexByte accepts as 1 or 2 hex digits with optional 0x prefix; anything else refuses the press with a warning and sends nothing.",
    "input_select and audio_select use logical input ids (computer1 ... sdi4); the module tries several hex terminal codes per input (INPUT_LOGICAL in src/nec/constants.ts). The audio_select action uses only the first code of the chosen input.",
    "Notable defaults of the source: power defaults to 'on', the other on/off/toggle actions to 'toggle'. The power action can be refused by the module (powerOnRefusal, powerOffRefusal) during the power-off lockout, which is set by the module config (powerOffLockout, default 65 s).",
    "send_raw takes command bytes as hex text split on whitespace or commas, without length and checksum, and can send any command the projector accepts. lan_name sends the typed text as the projector name; the label says max 16 characters, the action itself declares no limit.",
    "The input_active feedback compares the decoded input name (INPUT_NAME_CHOICES, which differ from the logical input ids of the action) with the polled state, so 'HDMI' matches both HDMI 1 and HDMI 2. Feedbacks other than input_active have no options.",
    "Presets, variables and the polling/feedback logic are not catalogued."
  ],
